-- title:
--   Auxiliary-level fixed field is the k₀-rational level-q field
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and let $M'\neq 0$ be an integer divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$; assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb Q$-field generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,(j)$ for $d\mid M'$ is contained in $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M',\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,n\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/n^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/n)^\times$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$, let $K$ be the $k_0$-subfield of $k_0((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}((q\ell)^2M',\mathrm{levelH}(q\ell)M')$, let $G\le \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ be generated by all $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell)\,\xi\,(q\ell)\,((q\ell)^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}(q\ell)M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ (so $\tau$ transforms ratios of integrally $q$-expanded modular forms of that level as the slash action by $\mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)\gamma^{-1}$ does, after any coefficient map $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$), and let $K_0=K^G$. Then, with $k_0$ acting on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ through $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ whose members are exactly the elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in (the image of) $k_0$, there is a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\sim}F_0$ such that (1) for all $f\in K_0$ the coefficientwise extension of $f$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equals $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,\ell$ applied to $\varphi f$, and (2) for every $g\in\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'\subseteq\mathbb Q((T))$ such that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell$ of the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K$ and the resulting element lies in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends it to the image of the coefficientwise extension of $g$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ under the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$.
--
--   This is the descent step identifying the fixed field of the $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms on the auxiliary level-$q\ell$ function field with the field of level-$q$ modular functions having $k_0$-rational $q$-expansion coefficients, the isomorphism being normalised by the $\ell$-expansion and by its effect on level-$M'$ functions with rational coefficients. It feeds the framed version [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_qExpand_framed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_qExpand_framed), and through it the arithmetic Galois description of the Jacobian used later.
